	<key>PayloadDescription</key>
	<string>Keeps the Family Site Blocker add-on installed and switched on in Firefox, for every account on this Mac. Firefox installs the newest signed version from https://adviseworn.github.io/family-site-blocker-updates/family-site-blocker.xpi, keeps it up to date, and nobody can turn it off or remove it there. Firefox also gets its own copy of the add-on’s built-in list of sites (whole adult domains such as .porn and .xxx, and the sites people visit most), which keeps blocking them when add-ons don’t run, as in Troubleshoot Mode. Private windows, Troubleshoot Mode from Firefox’s menus, about:config and Refresh Firefox, which could get round it, are turned off. Settings that other programs, such as another blocker, give Firefox for their own add-ons stay in force. Only an administrator can remove this profile.</string>
	<key>PayloadDisplayName</key>
	<string>Family Site Blocker for Firefox</string>
	<key>PayloadIdentifier</key>
	<string>local.parental-controls.family-site-blocker.firefox</string>
